==English==
{{slim-wikipedia}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰebʰ-}}
From {{der|en|enm|given}}, from {{der|en|non|gefa||to give}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*gebaną||to give}}. Merged with native Middle English {{m|enm|yiven}}, {{m|enm|ȝeven}}, from {{der|en|ang|ġiefan}}, from the same Proto-Germanic source (compare the obsolete inherited English {{glossary|doublet}} {{doublet|en|yive|notext=1}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|gĭv}}, {{IPA|en|/ɡɪv/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-give.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-to give.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪv|s=1}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|gives|giving|gave|given}}

# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To [[move]], [[shift]], [[provide]] something abstract or concrete to someone or something or somewhere.
## To [[transfer]] one's possession or holding of (something) to (someone).
##: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:give}}
##: {{ant|en|get|obtain|receive|take}}
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' him my coat.}}
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' my coat to the beggar.}}
##: {{ux|en|When they asked, I '''gave''' my coat.}}
## To make a [[present]] or [[gift]] of.
##: {{ux|en|I'm going to '''give''' my wife a necklace for her birthday.}}
##: {{ux|en|She '''gave''' a pair of shoes to her husband for their anniversary.}}
##: {{ux|en|He '''gives''' of his energies to the organization.}}
## To [[pledge]].
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' him my word that I'd protect his children.}}
## To [[provide]] (something) to (someone), to [[allow]] or [[afford]].
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' them permission to miss tomorrow's class.}}
##: {{ux|en|Please '''give''' me some more time.}}
## To cause (a sensation or feeling) to exist in (the specified person, or the target, audience, etc).
##: {{ux|en|It '''gives''' me a lot of pleasure to be here tonight.}}
##: {{ux|en|The fence '''gave''' me an electric shock.}}
##: {{ux|en|My mother-in-law '''gives''' me nothing but grief.}}
##: {{ux|en|It's '''giving''' me bad vibes.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|date=2022-10-25|author1=Medina Azaldin|author2=ELLE Beauty Team|title=30 Halloween Nail Art Trends To Get You In The Mood For Trick Or Treat|passage=[subtitle:] It's '''giving''' Wednesday Addams at the salon...}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2023-02-21|author=Lakita Wilson|title=Last Chance Dance|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9780593525630|page=81
|text="The outfit is '''giving''' me eighties fitness video vibes, but you wear it well." }}
## To [[carry out]] (a physical interaction) with (something).
##: {{ux|en|I want to '''give''' you a kiss.}}
##: {{ux|en|She '''gave''' him a hug.}}
##: {{ux|en|I'd like to '''give''' the tire a kick.}}
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' the boy a '''push''' on the swing.}}
##: {{ux|en|She '''gave''' me a wink afterwards, so I knew she was joking.}}
##* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|page=68|passage=Then came a maid with hand-bag and shawls, and after her a tall young lady. She stood for a moment holding her skirt above the grimy steps, with something of the stately pose which Richter has '''given''' his Queen Louise on the stairway,{{...}}.}}
## To pass (something) into (someone's hand, etc.).
##: {{ux|en|'''Give''' me your hand.}}
##: {{ux|en|On entering the house, he '''gave''' his coat to the doorman.}}
## To cause (a disease or condition) in, or to transmit (a disease or condition) to.
##: {{ux|en|My boyfriend '''gave''' me chlamydia.}}
##: {{ux|en|He was convinced that it was his alcoholism that '''gave''' him cancer.}}
##* {{RQ:Temple Miscellanea|part=3|page=331|passage=Study '''gives''' strength to the mind; conversation, grace: the first apt to '''give''' stiffness, the other suppleness: one '''gives''' substance and form to the statue, the other polishes it.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[provide]], as, a [[service]] or a [[broadcast]].
#: {{ux|en|They're '''giving''' my favorite show!}}
