#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|II|viii|page=171|passage=But there the duke was '''given''' to understand&nbsp;/ That in a gondola were seen together&nbsp;/ Lorenzo and his amorous Jessica.}}
# To cause (someone) to have; produce in (someone); [[effectuate]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1997|author=Jim Smoke|title=How a Man Measures Success|page=82|passage="Can do" gives me a choice, while "should do" '''gives''' me a complex.}}
